1
00:00:00,129 --> 00:00:02,459
(Amy:)Wil, that was a little wooden.

2
00:00:03,966 --> 00:00:06,166
- Wooden?
- Don't worry, it wasn't terrible.

3
00:00:06,335 --> 00:00:10,035
(Amy:)Just this time,
try to say it the way people sound.

4
00:00:11,908 --> 00:00:13,538
(Amy:)And action.

5
00:00:14,310 --> 00:00:16,010
(Sheldon:)My friend Wil Wheaton.

6
00:00:16,179 --> 00:00:18,509
Hi, thanks for having me.
I'm excited to be here.

7
00:00:18,681 --> 00:00:23,051
- So, Wil, what do you have for us first?
- Well, this is an exciting one.

8
00:00:23,219 --> 00:00:25,649
(Wil:)This is the flag
of the United Federation of Planets.

9
00:00:25,822 --> 00:00:28,622
(Wil:)- Now, what's interesting about this flag...
- Cut.

10
00:00:29,625 --> 00:00:33,565
- What was wrong with that?
- It's called Fun With Flags.

11
00:00:33,729 --> 00:00:37,429
(Amy:)They're not at half-mast. Nobody died.
Let's try and keep it upbeat.

12
00:00:38,601 --> 00:00:41,971
Um, no offense,
but I've been acting since I was a kid.

13
00:00:42,138 --> 00:00:44,568
(Wil:)I can handle a web show
without a lot of direction.

14
00:00:44,740 --> 00:00:45,830
(Sheldon:)It's true.

15
00:00:46,008 --> 00:00:50,038
(Sheldon:)In 1982 Wil played the voice
of Martin the mouse in The Secret of NIMH.

16
00:00:50,580 --> 00:00:52,010
(Sheldon:)You moved me.

17
00:00:53,049 --> 00:00:54,419
(Amy:)You'll have to forgive me.

18
00:00:54,584 --> 00:00:57,744
(Amy:)This is my first time directing.
I just want it to be good.

19
00:00:57,954 --> 00:00:59,214
- So do I.
- Great.

